hip-virtual-mem: an addition to intel/llvm v7.2.0, applied by tools/intel_llvm_build.py.

The HIP adapter answered every virtual memory call (urVirtualMem*, urPhysicalMem*) with
UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE and reported no virtual memory support, so SYCL's ext_oneapi_virtual_mem was not there
on AMD GPUs: XeStrata's --vram-elastic (the expert cache in segments it gives back for an image job and maps
again after it) and the elastic K/V (--kv-grow) fell back to one allocation.  HIP has the same virtual memory
management as CUDA (hipMemAddressReserve, hipMemCreate, hipMemMap, hipMemSetAccess and the others), so the
calls are implemented with it as the CUDA adapter implements them with CUDA's, and the device reports the
support HIP's hipDeviceAttributeVirtualMemoryManagementSupported says it has.
---
